      "severity": "nit",
      "code_change_required": false,
      "note": "HEAD /ping returns 200, not 404. Express auto-registers HEAD for every app.get(). Suppressing it would require the app.all() guard ADR-002 forbids and would contradict RFC 9110 section 9.3.2. Remedy is wording in design section 3.4."
    },
    {
      "id": "F-2",
      "source": "senior_code_review",
      "severity": "nit",
      "code_change_required": false,
      "note": "Design section 3.2 states catch-all arity 3; ADR-004 normative code is arity 2. Code follows ADR-004 and is correct. Load-bearing constraint is negative: a 4-arity catch-all would be reclassified as error middleware and unmatched requests would hang."
    },
    {
      "id": "SEC-01",
      "source": "security_review",
      "severity": "info",
      "code_change_required": false,
      "note": "Node HTTP parser answers malformed framing with a bare 400, no Content-Type, below the Express layer. Discloses nothing."
    },
